  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Unsettled weather will persist throughout this \nweek with daily chances of showers and thunderstorms.\n\nOutflow boundary from this afternoon's storms has stalled from \nCharleston WV (KCRW) to Bluefield WV (KBLF) to Mount Airy NC \n(KMWK) this evening. Watching for storms to form and track along\nthis boundary tonight. Estimated time for storms to enter our \nfar western counties would be between 11P and 1A.\n\nUpper pattern keeps a trough from the mid-Atlantic north into\nthe Canada, with ridge set up from Texas to the southeast coast.\n\nSeveral embedded vorts, some convective induced will track from\nthe Ohio Valley/Midwest into our area for the next couple of\ndays. Strong to severe storms possible Tuesday with good shear,\nbut limiting factor could be morning convection and upper clouds\nthat may limit sunshine. Still any sunshine will lead to SBCAPEs\nin the 1000-2000 J/kg range, and seems enough to overall keep\npops higher over WV per model trends. Temps/dewpoints were\nlowered from NBM Tuesday with downsloping and cloud cover.\n\nAlthough convective activity diminishes a little in intensity \nand coverage towards the end of this week, sufficient \ninstability and orographical lift will ensure that storm chances\nlinger throughout the upcoming weekend.",
